---
title: Kung Pao Chicken (Gong Bao Ji Ding 宫保鸡丁)
description: A classic Sichuan stir-fry dish consisting of diced chicken, peanuts, and chili peppers in a sweet, sour, and savory sauce.
prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 10 minutes
servings: 4
tags:
  - chicken
  - chinese
  - sichuan
course: Main
---

== Preparation ==

Dice @chicken breast or thigh{400%g} into small bite-sized cubes.

Marinate the chicken with @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @Shaoxing wine{1%tbsp}, @cornstarch{1%tsp}, and a pinch of @white pepper{}. Let it sit for ~{15%minutes}.

Cut @dried chilies{10} into halves and discard the seeds.

Chop @scallions{2} into sections, mince @garlic{3%cloves}, and slice @ginger{3%slices}.

Prepare the Kung Pao sauce: In a bowl, mix @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @dark soy sauce{1/2%tsp}, @black vinegar{1%tbsp}, @sugar{1%tbsp}, @chicken stock or water{2%tbsp}, and @cornstarch{1%tsp}.

== Cooking ==

Heat @oil{2%tbsp} in a #wok{} over high heat. Add the marinated chicken and stir-fry until cooked through and slightly browned. Remove the chicken and set aside.

In the same wok, add a little more oil if needed. Fry @Sichuan peppercorns{1%tsp} over low heat until fragrant, then optionally remove them.

Add the dried chilies and fry until they start to darken.

Add the minced garlic, sliced ginger, and scallion sections, and stir-fry until aromatic.

Return the cooked chicken to the wok and toss well.

Give the prepared Kung Pao sauce a quick stir to dissolve the cornstarch, then pour it into the wok. Stir rapidly until the sauce thickens and coats the chicken evenly.

== Finishing ==

Turn off the heat, stir in @roasted peanuts{1/2%cup} and a drizzle of @sesame oil{1%tsp}.

Serve immediately with steamed rice.
